  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Advancing Community-based Women Peace and Security (WPS) Implementation Mechanisms in Thailand</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to strengthen community-based Women, Peace, and Security (WPS) mechanisms in Thailand&#x2019;s border provinces of Trat and Tak (Mae Sot district) by enhancing the leadership and meaningful participation of women and women-led organisations in conflict prevention, peacebuilding, and emergency response. It seeks to localise the WPS agenda in alignment with Thailand&#x2019;s commit-ments under the ASEAN Regional Plan of Action (RPA) on WPS, contributing to inclusive governance and gender-responsive approaches to conflict prevention, peacebuilding, sustained peace, and resili-ence in fragile border communities</narrative>
  </description>
